        body: "Assume rough numbers: PMT has **25% SoV** with ads built from real student stories, **IQ 1.3**. A competitor has **45% SoV** with generic \"Classes available! Book now!\" ads, **IQ 0.7**.\n\n- PMT: 25% × 1.3 = **32.5% share of mind**\n- Competitor: 45% × 0.7 = **31.5% share of mind**\n\nPMT spends a bit over half as much and owns slightly more mental real estate.\n\n**Planning question:** PMT wants a 40% share of mind. At IQ 1.3 that takes 40 ÷ 1.3 ≈ 31% SoV. At IQ 1.0 it would take 40%. Raising IQ from 1.0 to 1.3 is worth nine points of share of voice, which in a market where every point costs money is a big budget saving, earned by writing."
