          rubric: ["Audits at least four kinds of signal (number, word, color, image, name)", "Names the association each one triggers, not just the literal meaning", "Rewrites only what sends the wrong signal", "The rewrite's hidden messages line up with the brand association you want"],
          model: "**Ad (gym prospect):** \"Join now! Only $9.99/month! No commitment!\" Neon yellow, a shredded bodybuilder stock photo.\n\n**Audit:** *$9.99* says bargain bin and crowded. *No commitment* says nobody here cares if you quit. Neon yellow says discount store. The bodybuilder says \"not for people like you\" to a 45-year-old beginner.\n\n**Rewrite:** \"Your first 30 days, coached. Real people, real Sacramento mornings.\" Deep green and warm light, with a photo of a real member in her 40s laughing mid-workout. Now it says belonging, being looked after and \"people like me.\""
